 of a 7-2  decision that makes clear that this was  not a close call I am not at all clear  what arguments he will try to raise but  it does mean that there'll be some  additional court appearances some  additional arguments in briefs filed I  think that the district court is very  likely to take its cue from the Supreme  Court and to order that the financial  records be released to to Vance now it's  important to bear in mind that doesn't  mean that the American public and the  world at large going to be able to see  those records what points in favor of  the Manhattan district attorney is that  grand jury proceedings are secret and so  the material that mizar's  will have to produce now will very  likely not see the light of day because  it's very important to protect that  grand jury secrecy but what it does mean  is that the president and the Trump  Organization can now be more thoroughly  investigated by a Manhattan grand jury  to see if any crimes were committed  right one of your speakers earlier said  that it won't result results in the  president being indicted hmm I'm not so  sure about that if there is clear  evidence of criminality in the  president's behavior or the behavior of  the Trump Organization  especially in that case there is  actually no constitutional principle  that says that a sitting president can't  be indicted he can certainly be  investigated and very possibly he could  be indicted before he leaves office  depending on what the grand jury finds  number one rule expect the unexpected  with this president isn't it Claire  Finkelstein always a pleasure talking to  you thank you thank you for having me
 

